<p id="S6.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, since <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(E)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(E)=0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S6.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{1}(\varphi^{*}\Omega_{{\mathbb{P}}^{3}}|{{}_{S_{0}}}(L))\leq\operatorname{cork}\mu," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>cork</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\varphi^{*}\Omega_{{\mathbb{P}}^{3}}|{{}_{S_{0}}}(L))\leq\operatorname{cork}\mu,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
