</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#S6.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>), (<a href="#S6.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a>) and (<a href="#S6.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a>), we see that we obtain the desired inequality <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\Omega_{S}(L))\leq 6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\Omega_{S}(L))\leq 6</annotation></semantics></math> if we prove that</span></p>
<table id="S6.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(3L-4E)=5" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(3L-4E)=5</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S6.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{cork}\mu=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cork</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{cork}\mu=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove (<a href="#S6.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.8</span></a>), note that the evaluation map <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(E)\otimes{\mathcal{O}}_{S}\to{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(E)\otimes{\mathcal{O}}_{S}\to{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(E)</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective as <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E|</annotation></semantics></math> is base point free and has kernel <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(-E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(-E)</annotation></semantics></math>. Twisting by <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(L-E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(L-E)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.Ex19.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="23.02" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-11.069600110696001px" version="1.1" viewBox="7.61 11.07 409.97 23.02" width="409.97"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 7.610350076103501 23.02480961287749) translate(0,3.46) translate(7.61,0)"><g transform="translate(-7.61,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex19.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{0\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{0\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 7.610371189690138 -0.27673578005007266 L 7.610371189690138 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(40.82,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 7.610371189690138 -0.27673578005007266 L 40.819150408191504 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 40.819150408191504 -0.27673578005007266 L 40.819150408191504 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(40.82,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.89em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="67.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex19.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(L-2E)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(L-2E)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 116.77078114054717 -0.27673578005007266 L 116.77078114054717 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(149.98,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 116.77078114054717 -0.27673578005007266 L 149.97956035904852 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 149.97956035904852 -0.27673578005007266 L 149.97956035904852 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(149.98,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.32em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="115.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex19.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{H^{0}(E)\otimes{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(L-E)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{H^{0}(E)\otimes{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(L-E)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 273.45736788502535 -0.27673578005007266 L 273.45736788502535 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(306.67,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 273.45736788502535 -0.27673578005007266 L 306.6661471035267 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 306.6661471035267 -0.27673578005007266 L 306.6661471035267 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(306.67,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.82em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="38.96"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex19.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(L)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{O}}_{S}(L)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 353.9253848212973 -0.27673578005007266 L 353.9253848212973 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(387.14,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 353.9253848212973 -0.27673578005007266 L 387.1341640397987 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 387.1341640397987 -0.27673578005007266 L 387.1341640397987 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(387.14,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex19.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking cohomology and using the fact that <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(L-E)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(L-E)=0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L-E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L-E</annotation></semantics></math> is big and nef by Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmdefinition2" title="Lemma 6.2. ‣ 6.1.2. Extension of elliptic curves to the Grassmannian 
            
              
                G
                
                  
                    
                    
                    
                  
                  
                    (
                    
                      
                      V
                      6
                    
                    ,
                    2
                    ) ‣ 6.1. Linear sections of 
          
            
              G
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  (
                  
                    
                    V
                    6
                  
                  ,
                  2
                  )
                
              
            
          
         and elliptic pencils ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>, we obtain that <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{cork}\mu=h^{1}(L-2E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cork</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{cork}\mu=h^{1}(L-2E)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L-2E).L=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L-2E).L=4</annotation></semantics></math>, whence <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}(L-2E)=h^{0}(2E-L)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}(L-2E)=h^{0}(2E-L)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is ample.
Similarly, <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(L-2E)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(L-2E)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L-2E).(L-E)=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L-2E).(L-E)=-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L-E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L-E</annotation></semantics></math> is nef.
Since <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L-2E)^{2}=-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L-2E)^{2}=-6</annotation></semantics></math>, Riemann–Roch yields <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(L-2E)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(L-2E)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and (<a href="#S6.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.8</span></a>) is proved.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove (<a href="#S6.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a>), note that <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3L-4E)^{2}=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3L-4E)^{2}=6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}(3L-4E)=h^{0}(4E-3L)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}(3L-4E)=h^{0}(4E-3L)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4E-3L).E&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4E-3L).E&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is nef. Hence, (<a href="#S6.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a>) is equivalent to
<math id="S6.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(3L-4E)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(3L-4E)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">To get a contradiction, assume that <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(3L-4E)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(3L-4E)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx18" title="" class="ltx_ref">KL07</a>]</cite>, there exists an effective divisor <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}=-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}=-2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k:=-\Delta.(3L-4E)\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k:=-\Delta.(3L-4E)\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta.L&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta.L&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is ample, we must have</span></p>
<table id="S6.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta.E\geq 2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta.E\geq 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">One computes <math id="S6.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3L-4E-k\Delta)^{2}=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3L-4E-k\Delta)^{2}=6</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S6.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3L-4E-k\Delta).(L-E)=7-k\Delta.(L-E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3L-4E-k\Delta).(L-E)=7-k\Delta.(L-E)</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Hodge index theorem,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="24=(3L-4E-k\Delta)^{2}\cdot(L-E)^{2}\leq\left[7-k\Delta.(L-E)\right]^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24=(3L-4E-k\Delta)^{2}\cdot(L-E)^{2}\leq\left[7-k\Delta.(L-E)\right]^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">whence the only possibilities</span></p>
<ul id="S6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(I)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta.(L-E)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta.(L-E)=0</annotation></semantics></math>; or</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(II)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I2.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta.(L-E)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta.(L-E)=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I2.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">In case (I) we find <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L-E-\Delta)^{2}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L-E-\Delta)^{2}=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L-E-\Delta).(L-E)=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L-E-\Delta).(L-E)=4</annotation></semantics></math>, whence <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(L-E-\Delta)\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(L-E-\Delta)\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> by Riemann–Roch and Serre duality. By (<a href="#S6.E9" title="In Proof. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.9</span></a>) we have <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E+\Delta)^{2}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E+\Delta)^{2}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, whence also <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(E+\Delta)\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(E+\Delta)\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> by Riemann–Roch. But then <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(L-E-\Delta)h^{0}(E+\Delta)\geq 9=8+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(L-E-\Delta)h^{0}(E+\Delta)\geq 9=8+1</annotation></semantics></math>, contradicting Brill–Noether generality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">In case (II) we have <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta.L=\Delta.E+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta.L=\Delta.E+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2=\Delta.(3L-4E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2=\Delta.(3L-4E)</annotation></semantics></math>, which together yield <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta.E=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta.E=5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta.L=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta.L=6</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L-E-\Delta)^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L-E-\Delta)^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L-E-\Delta).L=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L-E-\Delta).L=3</annotation></semantics></math>, whence
<math id="S6.SS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(L-E-\Delta)\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(L-E-\Delta)\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> by Riemann–Roch and Serre duality. Moreover,
<math id="S6.SS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E+\Delta)^{2}=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E+\Delta)^{2}=8</annotation></semantics></math>, whence <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(E+\Delta)\geq 6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(E+\Delta)\geq 6</annotation></semantics></math> by Riemann–Roch. Similarly, to the previous case, we obtain a contradiction to Brill–Noether generality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that (<a href="#S6.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a>) holds and finishes the proof of the proposition.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S6.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\dots,9\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\dots,9\}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S6.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> be as in the previous subsection and</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p">let <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the moduli space of triples as in the introduction. Note that <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is birational to the open part of the tautological <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{8}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle over <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of pairs <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,C)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[S]\in{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[S]\in{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[C]</annotation></semantics></math> representing a smooth curve in <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L|</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the generator class of square <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>14</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i+1}}\subset{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i+1}}\subset{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S6.SS3.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\ldots,8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\ldots,8\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.SS3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}_{8}:{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}\to{\mathcal{M}}_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}_{8}:{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}\to{\mathcal{M}}_{8}</annotation></semantics></math> be the moduli map.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmdefinition10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmdefinition10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 6.10</span></span><span id="S6.Thmdefinition10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmdefinition10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmdefinition10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmdefinition10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each <math id="S6.Thmdefinition10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\ldots,9\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\ldots,9\}</annotation></semantics></math>, a general fiber of <math id="S6.Thmdefinition10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}_{8}</annotation></semantics></math> has dimension <math id="S6.Thmdefinition10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{0,6-i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{0,6-i\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmdefinition9" title="Proposition 6.9. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.9</span></a>, the fiber of <math id="S6.SS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{0}}_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{0}}_{8}</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth and <math id="S6.SS3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional at any point <math id="S6.SS3.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,C)\in{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{9}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,C)\in{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{9}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix such an <math id="S6.SS3.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,C)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">We will show that there exists a chain of irreducible components <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\subset(m_{8}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}})^{-1}([C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\subset(m_{8}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}})^{-1}([C])</annotation></semantics></math> of the fiber of <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{8}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{8}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\dots,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\dots,5\}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, containing <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,C)\in{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{9}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,C)\in{\mathcal{P}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{9}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,C)\in F_{5}\subsetneq F_{4}\subsetneq\dots\subsetneq F_{1}\subsetneq F_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>⊊</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>⊊</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊊</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊊</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,C)\in F_{5}\subsetneq F_{4}\subsetneq\dots\subsetneq F_{1}\subsetneq F_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, there exist <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surfaces <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}\in{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}\backslash{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}\in{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}\backslash{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\dots,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\dots,5\}</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim F_{0}=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim F_{0}=6</annotation></semantics></math> by Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmdefinition9" title="Proposition 6.9. ‣ 6.3. The moduli map ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.9</span></a>, the dimension of <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6-i</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.SS3.p18.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\dots,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\dots,5\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the proposition will follow.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">By construction, <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>) is the intersection of <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(V_{6},2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(V_{6},2)</annotation></semantics></math> with a <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{8}</annotation></semantics></math> (respectively a <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{7}</annotation></semantics></math>) in <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{14}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>14</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{14}</annotation></semantics></math>. The dual <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{8}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we henceforth call <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(S)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(S)}</annotation></semantics></math>, intersects the dual <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(2,V_{6})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(2,V_{6})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math> points, call them <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\ldots,x_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\ldots,x_{9}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the dual <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{7}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we henceforth call <math id="S6.SS3.p19.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{6}_{(C)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{6}_{(C)}</annotation></semantics></math>, contains
<math id="S6.SS3.p19.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(S)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(S)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">By construction, the nine points <math id="S6.SS3.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\ldots,x_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\ldots,x_{9}</annotation></semantics></math> span <math id="S6.SS3.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(S)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(S)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we may find inside <math id="S6.SS3.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{6}_{(C)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{6}_{(C)}</annotation></semantics></math> a set of six additional hyperplanes
<math id="S6.SS3.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS3.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\ldots,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\ldots,5\}</annotation></semantics></math> containing precisely <math id="S6.SS3.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> of the points
<math id="S6.SS3.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\ldots,x_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\ldots,x_{9}</annotation></semantics></math>; in particular <math id="S6.SS3.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> intersects <math id="S6.SS3.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(2,V_{6})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(2,V_{6})</annotation></semantics></math> in precisely <math id="S6.SS3.p20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> points.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote by <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{8}_{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{8}_{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> the dual <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{8}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{5}_{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{8}_{(i)}\cap G(V_{6},2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{8}_{(i)}\cap G(V_{6},2)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surface <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and precisely <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> elliptic pencils of degree <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> (and mutually intersecting in <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> points) by Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmdefinition4" title="Corollary 6.4. ‣ 6.1.2. Extension of elliptic curves to the Grassmannian 
            
              
                G
                
                  
                    
                    
                    
                  
                  
                    (
                    
                      
                      V
                      6
                    
                    ,
                    2
                    ) ‣ 6.1. Linear sections of 
          
            
              G
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  (
                  
                    
                    V
                    6
                  
                  ,
                  2
                  )
                
              
            
          
         and elliptic pencils ‣ 6. K3 surfaces of genus 8 ‣ Brill–Noether general K3 surfaces with the maximal number of elliptic pencils of minimal degree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>. As the nine elliptic pencils together with <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> generate <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{N}}_{9}\subset\mathop{\rm Pic}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⊂</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">Pic</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{N}}_{9}\subset\mathop{\rm Pic}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have that <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and the
<math id="S6.SS3.p21.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> elliptic pencils generate <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}\subset\mathop{\rm Pic}(S_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⊂</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">Pic</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}\subset\mathop{\rm Pic}(S_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, whence
<math id="S6.SS3.p21.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}\in{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}\backslash{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}\in{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}\backslash{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each pair <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{i},C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{i},C)</annotation></semantics></math> therefore lies in <math id="S6.SS3.p21.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\backslash F_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\backslash F_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmdefinition11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmdefinition11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6.11</span></span><span id="S6.Thmdefinition11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\ldots,9\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\ldots,9\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the codimension of the image of the moduli map <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>𝔑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{{\mathfrak{N}}_{i}}_{8}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{0,i-6\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{0,i-6\}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, a general curve of genus <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> is a linear section of a <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surface such that precisely six out of its <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>14</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{1}_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>5</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{1}_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>s are induced by elliptic pencils on the <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surface. Moreover, there is a codimension <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> family of curves lying on a <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surface such that precisely <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6+k</annotation></semantics></math> of its <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{1}_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>5</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{1}_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>s are induced by elliptic pencils on the <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surface for <math id="S6.Thmdefinition11.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,2,3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,2,3\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmdefinition12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmdefinition12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 6.12</span></span><span id="S6.Thmdefinition12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One can ask similar questions for <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surfaces of higher even genus. For instance, how many elliptic pencils of minimal degree exist on a Brill–Noether general <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surface? But the methods in this article cannot be applied to <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surfaces of higher genus. Indeed, let <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a Brill–Noether general curve of even genus <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\geq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\geq 10</annotation></semantics></math>. Note on the one hand that the curve <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> does not lie on a <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surface and on the other hand that the (finite) number of pencils of minimal degree on <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is bigger that <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="19" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>19</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">19</annotation></semantics></math> (the maximal rank of the Picard lattice of a smooth <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surface). Furthermore, a characterization of Brill–Noether general <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K3</annotation></semantics></math> surfaces is only known for <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\leq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\leq 10</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmdefinition12.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
